1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,808
Business Case 07 begins when required interview sessions complete and
scorecard work becomes due.

2
00:00:06,808 --> 00:00:12,157
An authorized human records an attributed decision using independent,
versioned evidence.

3
00:00:12,157 --> 00:00:14,588
The governed record is APP-DEMO-001.

4
00:00:14,588 --> 00:00:19,451
The accountable actors are Interviewer, Recruiter, Hiring Manager,
Decision Owner.

5
00:00:19,451 --> 00:00:26,745
This demonstration uses synthetic browser-memory data and creates no
database, provider, message or external-system effect.

6
00:00:26,745 --> 00:00:31,343
The action-level data-flow diagram defines 4 processes before product
navigation.

7
00:00:31,343 --> 00:00:39,620
Every process identifies the actor, screen, action, input, output,
business object, event, governed store, rule, denial and recovery.

8
00:00:39,620 --> 00:00:44,218
The highlighted path keeps each business grain and version distinct.

9
00:00:44,218 --> 00:00:46,840
Process 1, Interviewer: Submit independent scorecard.

10
00:00:46,840 --> 00:00:53,396
The action rate rubric and cite evidence produces locked scorecard
version in the Evidence ledger.

11
00:00:53,396 --> 00:00:56,018
Process 2, Recruiter: Inspect evidence coverage.

12
00:00:56,018 --> 00:01:03,011
The action reconcile competencies and missing work produces coverage map
and blockers in the Decision ledger.

13
00:01:03,011 --> 00:01:06,070
Process 3, Hiring Manager: Run structured debrief.

14
00:01:06,070 --> 00:01:12,626
The action compare evidence and conflicts produces debrief conclusion
without ranking in the Decision ledger.

15
00:01:12,626 --> 00:01:15,685
Process 4, Decision Owner: Record human decision.

16
00:01:15,685 --> 00:01:22,678
The action select outcome and rationale produces attributed decision and
candidate-safe status in the Decision ledger.

17
00:01:22,678 --> 00:01:25,503
The actual product route is /hr/decisions/APP-DEMO-001.

18
00:01:25,503 --> 00:01:32,096
It presents evidence coverage and structured debrief in the surrounding
recruitment or onboarding workspace.

19
00:01:32,096 --> 00:01:43,868
The screen remains a wireframe, but its identifiers, current state,
navigation, data relationships and action boundaries match the business
contract used by the connected workbench.

20
00:01:43,868 --> 00:01:46,792
The seeded workbench follows record DEB-DEMO-001.

21
00:01:46,792 --> 00:02:01,896
Its governed fields are Interview plan, IP-DEMO-004 , v3; Scorecards,
4/4 submitted and locked; Competency coverage, 6/6 covered; Conflict
flags, 0 active; Debrief conclusion, Proceed to offer; Decision owner,
Maya Chen.

22
00:02:01,896 --> 00:02:11,153
Field classifications remain visible so the presenter can distinguish
public, internal, confidential and restricted projections for the active
persona.

23
00:02:11,153 --> 00:02:15,747
With Hiring Manager selected, we perform record attributed human
decision.

24
00:02:15,747 --> 00:02:20,799
The guard requires independent scorecards, competency coverage and
authority are complete.

25
00:02:20,799 --> 00:02:33,202
The state changes from Ready for debrief to Human decision recorded,
records HiringDecisionRecorded, writes to the Decision ledger, and
creates the handoff: Offer owner receives authorized decision.

26
00:02:33,202 --> 00:02:37,242
We now exercise the controlled exception: Simulate missing evidence.

27
00:02:37,242 --> 00:02:42,180
The prepared failure is System-design evidence missing; one scorecard
amended late.

28
00:02:42,180 --> 00:02:51,607
Unsupported downstream work stops, successful prior evidence remains
intact, and the state-change receipt assigns explicit recovery without
hiding the failed attempt.

29
00:02:51,607 --> 00:02:54,931
The owned recovery is Collect amendment and reconvene.

30
00:02:54,931 --> 00:02:59,086
It reuses the governed business context without duplicating completed
effects.

31
00:02:59,086 --> 00:03:04,487
The new receipt preserves previous state, current state, actor, event
and correlation key.

32
00:03:04,487 --> 00:03:14,044
The control center and handoff inbox then expose the same recovery
through evidence completeness, debrief age and amendment rate and
minimum-context next-actor work.

33
00:03:14,044 --> 00:03:16,118
Business Case 07 is complete.

34
00:03:16,118 --> 00:03:28,149
We demonstrated the level-two process contract, the actual product
route, governed field projections, the primary state transition, a
controlled exception, targeted recovery, causal dashboard evidence and
the next-actor handoff.

35
00:03:28,149 --> 00:03:32,713
An authorized human records an attributed decision using independent,
versioned evidence.

36
00:03:32,713 --> 00:03:37,276
Production identity, persistence, integrations and external delivery
remain separate implementation gates.
